meaning:
Meek flips a passage from Psalm 23:4:

Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,
I will fear no evil;
For You are with me;
Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me

However, Mill replaces “shadow of death” with “ladder in flex” (his gun is cocked—"ladder" is Philly slang for a clip) to change the meaning of the quoted psalm and to fit with the rhyme.
